# Richard's Dev Landing - Project Context

## Overview
Personal portfolio/landing page for Richard Pastenes, a web developer. The site showcases projects, experience, education, and provides a printable resume page.

**Live URL:** https://richard.pastenes.dev

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Version | Notes |
|-------|-----------|---------|-------|
| Framework | SvelteKit | 2.x | Vite-powered, Svelte 5 |
| UI Library | Svelte | 5.x | Runes API ($props, $derived, $state) |
| CMS | Sanity.io | v2.36.6 | Headless CMS, studio in `cms/` directory |
| CMS Client | @sanity/client | 6.x | GROQ queries, server-side fetching |
| Portable Text | @portabletext/svelte | 3.x | Rich text rendering |
| Image URLs | @sanity/image-url | 1.x | Sanity image URL builder |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS | 3.4.x | Utility-first CSS with PostCSS |
| Language | TypeScript | 5.5+ | Strict mode |
| Deployment | Netlify | - | @sveltejs/adapter-netlify |
| Node.js | v20.11.0 | - | Specified in .nvmrc |
| Package Manager | npm | - | ESM ("type": "module") |

## Sanity CMS Configuration
- **Project ID:** lpvkp4xx
- **Dataset:** production
- **Studio location:** `cms/` directory (runs on localhost:3333)
- **Sanity version:** v2.36.6 (legacy, v2 is EOL - upgrade planned in Phase 2)
- **Config file:** `cms/sanity.json` (JSON-based, pre-v3)

### Content Types (Sanity Schemas)
Located in `cms/schemas/`:
- `hero` — Hero section (title, intro text, social links, headshot image)
- `about` — About section (block content, technology tags)
- `project` — Portfolio projects (title, description, image, tags, links)
- `experience` — Work experience entries
- `education` — Education entries
- `achievment` — Achievement entries (note: typo in original schema name)
- `resume` — Resume/CV data
- `links` — Social/external links

